  "factor_name": "Trend Breadth Stability with Downside-Risk Scaling",
  "version": "2028-07-31",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "pct_change(close,60) * (2*rolling_mean(I[pct_change(close,1)>0],60)-1) / (sqrt(rolling_mean(min(pct_change(close,1),0)^2,60))+0.01), lagged 1 session",
    "description": "Ranks each asset by its lagged 60-session trend, multiplied by the persistence of positive daily returns and scaled by downside deviation. Positive breadth persistence rewards durable trends while downside-risk scaling limits noisy exposures. Cross-sectional ranking is used for portfolio construction."
